WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:16.090
Good afternoon, John. It is Thursday, January
11th. (sneezes twice)

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:21.619
So I was just watching my video from January
9th. I'm paying the price for not being commensurate

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:29.150
with my values. At some point, while in Detroit,
I met a really — like a tiny chicken. I

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.329
don't actually remember this tiny chicken
but I'm almost positive that we had an encounter,

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:42.810
because this tiny chicken has laid tiny eggs
in my head. One here. One here. One here and

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.810
one here.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.559
(sniffles)

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:55.519
Those tiny eggs are growing and hatching,
and the baby tiny chickens are feeding on

00:00:55.519 --> 00:01:04.070
my brain. They do everything that baby chickens
do. They're cute, they're fuzzy. They poop,

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:09.640
and they eat. They're eating my brain and
their poop is coming out my nose. Fucking

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.640
tiny chicken!

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.960
Tell me if you seen junk coming out of my
nose, because it'd be really embarrassing

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:23.329
to have that caught on video blog. No, it's
still there! Ahh, there we go. Ha ha! (sniffle)

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:27.950
No junk. No junk coming out of my nose. No.
I think that we should suggest some more punishments

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:30.549
so that we can choose between punishments.

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:35.710
Also, we can have people suggest punishments.
So far all we have is the 500 Miles punishment,

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.939
which I'd be totally okay of doing. Honestly,
I think it'd be fun.

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:47.930
So, punishments that I am suggesting today:
Grow your facial hair for one full week and

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.939
then wax your chin. Also, there's the Stick
A Needle In My Eye provision. Third on my

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:59.130
list of punishments that I'm suggesting for
today: Give yourself a mohawk. I kind of always

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.659
wanted to give myself a mohawk, and I'd really
like an excuse.

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:06.069
I've got a little bit of a problem, and I
was hoping that you or maybe one of our viewers

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:09.509
could help me out. I was going to Detroit,
right, so I figured I'd have a bunch of business

00:02:09.509 --> 00:02:13.880
cards printed up. I used an online service,
and I upload my files, and they sent me a

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:21.040
bunch of business cards. I like that. I like,
it's like a nice, sturdy card stock. And on

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.591
the back, it's supposed to be like this one,
which I got printed up at Kinko's. But this

00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:34.129
one, on the back, says this. And on the front,
says this.

00:02:34.129 --> 00:02:38.489
What am I supposed to do with this? Okay,
it's one thing to have one that does that...

00:02:38.489 --> 00:02:44.379
What about this many? This many, that are
the same on all the sides. What am I supposed

00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:51.439
to do with it? John, viewers: What do I do
with 100 three inch by one-and-a-half inch

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:57.069
cards that say 'ecogeek' on them? So far my
only idea is to tape them all over my face.

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:03.510
(sings) 'I would walk 500 miles and I would
walk 500 more'

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.819
See, this is — this is to me not a punishment.
I— I don't know. To me, it's not a punishment.

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:10.019
We sh— we need to come up with better punishments,
is what I'm saying.

